Subject: [PATCH 05120/11362] [outer-loop] headroom survey: FoVer is the
 oracle-distinct moat target; redirect PHASE D off MuSR

Operator 'try that next' (find an oracle-distinct domain with headroom where a verifier
beats the baseline). Decisive diagnostic on CACHED cross-domain pools (exp4305/4314), zero
generation:

- MuSR/math/CSP have NO oracle-distinct headroom (SC near-ceiling) -> the entire PHASE D null
  streak is a no-headroom artifact, not a method failure.
- FoVer is the ONLY oracle-distinct domain with real headroom: oracle@K 0.769 vs SC 0.269
  (+0.50). arc/arcgen also have headroom but are circular (executable oracle).
- The prior FoVer attempt (exp4305/4314) was CROSS-DOMAIN and collapsed: +0.231 lift reproduced
  identically by label-ablation = artifact (verdict cross_domain_selection_collapses_domain_bound).
  So FoVer headroom is real but UNCAPTURED.

Redirect (known-issues MANDATORY-NEXT): retire the MuSR-moat line; run IN-DOMAIN FoVer
verifier-selection vs tuned-SC (n>=150, verifier_is_oracle=false) with a MANDATORY label-ablation
negative control. Points the conductor's PHASE D (on codex, no Claude burn) at the right corpus.

